From 3f1d9634b8cae05331c69d80e4ab6eccec36e88b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:25:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 128/143] media: sunxi: cedar-ve: bound the STOP_PROC_INFO
 channel id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

IOCTL_STOP_PROC_INFO takes its channel id straight from the ioctl arg and
uses it to index ve_debug_proc_info.proc_buf[VE_DEBUGFS_MAX_CHANNEL] (16
entries) without any range check:

	channel_id = arg;
	ve_debug_proc_info.proc_buf[channel_id] = NULL;

channel_id is an unsigned char, so any value in 16..255 stores a NULL
pointer past the end of the array, corrupting the adjacent fields of the
global ve_debugfs_buffer (the data pointer, the lock_proc mutex) and the
BSS beyond it.  Any task that can open /dev/cedar_dev can trigger this
whenever CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is enabled (it is, in the shipped defconfig).

This is the same unvalidated-channel-id class fixed for IOCTL_COPY_PROC_INFO;
reject out-of-range ids here too.  Valid users (libcedarc only ever passes
ids 0..15) are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/media/platform/sunxi/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c
index 1f7ad6616..37609820a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c
@@ -1942,6 +1942,14 @@ static long compat_cedardev_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned
 					return 0;
 
 				channel_id = arg;
+				/*
+				 * channel_id comes straight from the ioctl arg and
+				 * indexes proc_buf[VE_DEBUGFS_MAX_CHANNEL]; reject
+				 * out-of-range ids to avoid an out-of-bounds store
+				 * past the array.
+				 */
+				if (channel_id >= VE_DEBUGFS_MAX_CHANNEL)
+					return -EINVAL;
 				ve_debug_proc_info.proc_buf[channel_id] = NULL;
 
 				break;
